## 5. TRI_TEST_PERSISTENT definition

A canonical baseline candidate is `TRI_TEST_PERSISTENT` only when:

1. it is shared by both TEST-24 orthography lanes;
2. it is `PERSISTENT` in all TEST-25 parameter variants;
3. it is `PERSISTENT` in all eight TEST-26 evidence-withholding subsamples.

The resulting stable core is:

| Layer | Canonical baseline | TRI_TEST_PERSISTENT | Fraction | Required | Persistence gate |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|:---:|
| QREF | 2 | 1 | 50.0000% | 80% | FAIL |
| QRELATION_LOCUS | 805 | 394 | 48.9441% | 80% | FAIL |
| QMOTIF | 1644 | 207 | 12.5912% | 75% | FAIL |
| QCONCEPT | 26 | 2 | 7.6923% | 75% | FAIL |

Exact stable QREF candidate:

```text
انه
```

Exact TRI_TEST_PERSISTENT QCONCEPT structural keys:

```text
حليم|رحيم
غفور|لرءوف
```

These are structural keys only. They are not semantic labels.

