| Layer | Mean novel count | Mean novel rate vs baseline | Maximum allowed | Gate |
|---|---:|---:|---:|:---:|
| QREF | 0.000 | 0.0000% | 5% | PASS |
| QRELATION_LOCUS | 0.000 | 0.0000% | 5% | PASS |
| QMOTIF | 0.625 | 0.0380% | 10% | PASS |
| QCONCEPT | 6.000 | 23.0769% | 10% | FAIL |

QCONCEPT produces on average `6` novel groupings per subsample, equal to `23.0769%` of its canonical baseline inventory.

## 7. Final decision under policy v1

```text
COMPLETE SNAPSHOT DECISION = DEFERRED
REASON = PREDECLARED_STABILITY_ACCEPTANCE_POLICY_NOT_MET
```

The reproducibility gates pass, but:

- all four layers fail the predeclared complete-snapshot TRI_TEST_PERSISTENT coverage threshold;
- QCONCEPT also fails the predeclared novel-candidate-rate threshold.

Therefore `DIVINE_ONTOLOGY_VNEXT_SNAPSHOT_1` must **not** be frozen as a complete ontology snapshot.

